note SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
note src/ufbi_ivmath.om: elementary functions accurate enough for the interval certificates.
note Composed after src/ufbi_math.om and before a certificate source.
note
note WHY THIS FILE EXISTS (review finding F1, 2026-11-22):
note   uSin64 in ufbi_math.om stops its Taylor series at x^15/15!. At |x| = pi/2 the omitted term is
note   (pi/2)^17/17! = 6.1e-12, larger than the certificates' inflation margin, so "upper bounds" built
note   from it were not upper bounds (ivHi(uCos64 0) < 1). ufbi_math.om is left unchanged so the GPU
note   check binaries keep their recorded hashes; certificates must use ivSin64 / ivCos64 instead.
note
note The Taylor remainder after degree 23 on the folded interval is bounded by (pi/2)^25/25!.
note scripts/ivmath_crosscheck.py samples binary64 reduction and evaluation against mpmath.
note Its thresholds are regression checks. A full enclosure proof also requires roundoff
note analysis of each composed expression, its argument range, and the quadrature.
note The certificate sources share the same absolute and relative padding below.

fn ivSin64 theta f64 to f64
pi = uPi
twopi = uTwoPi
halfpi = uHalfPi
k = long div theta twopi
x = sub theta mul f64 k twopi
while gt x pi bound 8
x = sub x twopi
end
while lt x neg pi bound 8
x = add x twopi
end
if gt x halfpi
x = sub pi x
end
if lt x neg halfpi
x = sub neg pi x
end
x2 = mul x x
s = f64 1.0f64
s = sub 1.0f64 div mul x2 s 506.0f64
s = sub 1.0f64 div mul x2 s 420.0f64
s = sub 1.0f64 div mul x2 s 342.0f64
s = sub 1.0f64 div mul x2 s 272.0f64
s = sub 1.0f64 div mul x2 s 210.0f64
s = sub 1.0f64 div mul x2 s 156.0f64
s = sub 1.0f64 div mul x2 s 110.0f64
s = sub 1.0f64 div mul x2 s 72.0f64
s = sub 1.0f64 div mul x2 s 42.0f64
s = sub 1.0f64 div mul x2 s 20.0f64
s = sub 1.0f64 div mul x2 s 6.0f64
ret mul x s
end

fn ivCos64 theta f64 to f64
ret ivSin64 add theta uHalfPi
end

fn ivLo x f64 to f64
m = add mul uAbs64 x 0.000000000001f64 0.0000000000001f64
ret sub x m
end

fn ivHi x f64 to f64
m = add mul uAbs64 x 0.000000000001f64 0.0000000000001f64
ret add x m
end
